course: dictionary
lesson: 10568
title: Unconscious: not awake, or not aware
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning the writer wants. Unconscious is one of these words. «When someone's life may be in danger, someone unconscious, you call 999 in the UK.» Here unconscious means not awake and not able to see, hear or feel, so the person needs help quickly.
explain: The second meaning is about doing something without noticing it. «An unconscious habit» is one you do without thinking, like tapping your pencil on the desk. The clue is the word habit: it is something you do again and again, often without deciding to.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning. Ask: is the person asleep or hurt and unable to respond, or is someone just doing something without noticing? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Unconscious means not awake and not able to see, hear or feel, for example after a bad bang on the head.
fact: Unconscious can also mean not aware: doing something without knowing or noticing it.
fact: «The recovery position» keeps the airway open in someone who is unconscious but breathing.
fact: In psychology, «the unconscious» is the part of the mind that has thoughts and feelings you do not notice.
fact: A word with two meanings is understood by its context: read the sentence, then choose the meaning that fits.
exercise: «The recovery position keeps the airway open in someone who is unconscious but breathing.» What does unconscious mean here? | Not thinking about it on purpose | Happy and full of energy | *Not awake and not able to see, hear or feel | Very tired after a long day at school
exercise: Mia says her nail biting is «an unconscious habit». What does unconscious suggest? | *Doing it without knowing or noticing | Doing it on purpose after careful thought | Doing it in a hospital | Doing it very loudly
exercise: «Someone not breathing, unconscious, badly bleeding, you call 999.» Which meaning fits unconscious best? | Calm and happy | Aware of everything around them | Careless about rules | *Not awake, not able to respond
test: What is the best way to check a meaning from context? | Look only at the first letter of the word | Skip the sentence forever | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Guess the longest answer
test: In psychology, what is the unconscious? | A kind of lamp | The part of the body that moves your legs | *The part of the mind with thoughts and feelings you do not notice | A type of emergency number
exam: When you find someone unconscious in the UK, what should you do first? | Pour water on their face | Walk away and wait for them to wake up | *Call 999 | Tell them a joke
